From: ANV15-51 local backport preparation
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86: acer-wmi: enable ANV15-51 monitoring and PWM

Backport ANV15-51 support by Justin Vargas from platform-drivers-x86.
The original change was subsequently reapplied under another object ID.

Linux 7.2.9 predates the split hwmon/platform_profile quirk fields.
Use its existing predator_v4 quirk field for those two capabilities.
Do not set the module parameter: that bypasses model-specific detection.

Retain the upstream CPU/GPU counts and PWM capability. Do not enable
legacy turbo/overclock features or change any fan WMI operations.
Compilation is not hardware validation of this backport or Auto recovery.

Link: https://github.com/kernelorg-mirror/linux_kernel_git_pdx86_platform-drivers-x86/commit/71019d2a13e0766ca174846e68dc5c0bde2e6494
Link: https://github.com/kernelorg-mirror/linux_kernel_git_pdx86_platform-drivers-x86/commit/9319f8ff83941d63658d230b3f02138764fceadc
---
 drivers/platform/x86/acer-wmi.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/acer-wmi.c b/drivers/platform/x86/acer-wmi.c
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/acer-wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/acer-wmi.c
@@ -466,6 +466,13 @@ static struct quirk_entry quirk_acer_predator_ph315_53 = {
 	.gpu_fans = 1,
 };
 
+static struct quirk_entry quirk_acer_nitro_anv15_51 = {
+	.cpu_fans = 1,
+	.gpu_fans = 1,
+	.predator_v4 = 1,
+	.pwm = 1,
+};
+
 static struct quirk_entry quirk_acer_predator_ph16_72 = {
 	.turbo = 1,
 	.cpu_fans = 1,
@@ -662,6 +669,15 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id acer_quirks[] __initconst = {
 		},
 		.driver_data = &quirk_acer_nitro_an515_58,
 	},
+	{
+		.callback = dmi_matched,
+		.ident = "Acer Nitro ANV15-51",
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "Acer"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "Nitro ANV15-51"),
+		},
+		.driver_data = &quirk_acer_nitro_anv15_51,
+	},
 	{
 		.callback = dmi_matched,
 		.ident = "Acer Predator PH315-53",
